  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Pakistan 2025 &#x2013; Strategic Action on Flood Risk Management and Spatial Planning</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan faces some of the highest disaster risk levels in the world. Because of its vulnerable socio-economic profile and multi-geographic positioning, the country is listed among those worst affected by extreme weather events due to climate change. In the framework of the Dutch Risk Reduction and Surge Support (DRRS) programme, the Netherlands Enterprise Agency RVO) strives to ignite debate and initiate a course of action focused on flood resilience and spatial planning. The goal is to form a &#x2018;coalition of the willing&#x2019; around the most promising elements of the white paper, starting with informal discussions and conversations, and appealing to the moral ambitions of key individuals within the system. By engaging effectively with key stakeholders, primarily the Government of Sindh and local communities, the aim is to promote the understanding, acceptance, and reinforcement of specific spatial planning applications for strengthening flood resilience in Sindh, ultimately leading to action planning and implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
